                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "816e24d5-8e76-496e-b3f9-7cbf581ecc6f",
                        "source_entry_id": "1588f296-7335-3664-9ecf-a91139afe1fd",
                        "source_sense_id": "2103ac71-6eae-3ca0-9606-5f563cd6b8f8",
                        "target_lang_word": "hanafuda",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hanafuda",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                        "entry_id": "b6fea3b3-0e10-3feb-a83b-6d16e31e4664",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small, rigid Japanese playing cards with colorful drawings of flowers and animals, a single deck consisting of 48 cards divided in 12 suits that each represent a month."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49547435-8e6a-47ae-b6b6-4b86b053f43f",
                                                "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                                "text": "Briefly, Sin described the Hanafuda playing cards and how he had adapted them to his own ends."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed43b7ea-9fa1-4242-b098-57dae7390ab7",
                                                "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                                "text": "On a different occasion, he was playing hanafuda in a mountain hut with several Japanese."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ee1e6ae-f494-4ebf-98a1-89a328a86ea1",
                                                "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                                "text": "“What’s hanafuda?” Sam asked.\n“Plastic cards. Quite small and thick, with flowers and scenes of nature,” Watanabe-san said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49ec4807-7494-4acf-a85e-1657cf65b31f",
                                                "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                                "text": "A pack of \"Hana-fuda\" consists of 48 cards, there being 12 different denominations or figures, and each such denomination or figure being represented by 4 cards of different face values; the figures on such 4 cards of the same denomination being the same, but having certain marks upon them to indicate the difference in their respective face values."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "403bcdd8-fd0f-48b1-8a37-6476a10a905e",
                                                "sense_id": "bbcab372-97b3-33a1-9c1a-06da9f5f40e7",
                                                "text": "Couldn't we play with hanafuda cards instead? I asked. I had a decent amount of experience with oichokabu or koi koi thanks to playing with my mom's family in the countryside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "70e891e6-2e25-4f99-96ce-91e77c76ae2b",
                        "source_entry_id": "1588f296-7335-3664-9ecf-a91139afe1fd",
